{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And your father, etc.</b> One needs to know what was the deception he practiced against him, for if he changed the terms outright, he would be called a robber." "<b>Or perhaps</b> Laban sensed from the very first time that he saw the flock bearing young in abundance of the kind pertaining to Jacob's portion, therefore he grew cunning and said: surely it is nothing. Therefore he would name one kind for him at the outset, and after the flock conceived he would change his mind between conception and birth and take for himself the kind he had named, and assign to Jacob a different kind. And therefore it is called only deception, for sometimes he would say one thing and sometimes, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:10.244901154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}